#
# gitleaks scans the FULL git history (the CI job checks out with
# fetch-depth: 0), so a finding in an old or since-deleted file keeps failing
# every run until it is listed here. Each line is a fingerprint:
#   <commit>:<file>:<rule>:<line>
#
# Real secrets must NEVER be silenced this way — rotate them instead. Nothing
# below is a credential; every entry was inspected before being added.

